  "starterCode": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_apply_custom_functions(records: list, src_col: str, new_col: str, transform_type: str = 'square') -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Apply Custom Transforms** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_apply_custom_functions(records: list, src_col: str, new_col: str, transform_type: str = 'square') -> list:\n    df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n    if transform_type == 'square':\n        df[new_col] = df[src_col].apply(lambda v: v ** 2)\n    elif transform_type == 'normalize':\n        m, s = df[src_col].mean(), df[src_col].std()\n        df[new_col] = df[src_col].apply(lambda v: round(float((v - m) / (s + 1e-12)), 4))\n    else:\n        df[new_col] = df[src_col].apply(lambda v: abs(v))\n    return df.to_dict(orient='records')\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
